; BZ tests the named register, during the branch; negative non-zero must NOT branch
LIL R1, 0
LIL R2, 0xFF
LIH R2, 0xFF        ; -1 (negative, non-zero)
LIL R5, 0
BZ R2, bad          ; not taken
ADDI R5, 1
BZ R1, good         ; taken
bad: LIL R6, 0xBA
HLT
good: LIL R0, 3
loop: ADDI R0, -1
ADDI R5, 1
BZ R0, out
JMP loop
out: LIL R4, 0          ; preceding ADD left Z set; BZ must re-test R2
ADD R4, R4, R4
BZ R2, bad
HLT
